ly defined and consistently used throughout the paper. The algorithm presentations, including the pseudocode for both the Pi-model and temporal ensembling, are self-contained, well-documented, and easy to follow. The variable names are clear, and the inputs and outputs are explicitly stated. The organization of the sections is logical, with a smooth transition from the introduction to the method, results, and related work. The writing is concise and readable, with no excessive jargon or redundancy.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-WRT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-005","SRC-007","SRC-011","SRC-013"],"review_text":"The mathematical notation is consistent and well-defined. The symbols used in the equations and pseudocode are clearly explained in the text. For example, the notation for the network outputs (z_i and z_tilde_i), the ensemble outputs (Z_i), and the momentum term (alpha) are all clearly defined. The derivations and explanations of the loss functions are well-explained, and the mathematical steps are easy to follow. The notation is used consistently throughout the paper, and there are no missing definitions or unexplained mathematical steps.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-NOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-016","SRC-017","SRC-020","SRC-024"],"review_text":"The tables in the paper are readable and provide clear comparisons of the results. The caption text for the figures is detailed and informative, providing a clear description of what the figures illustrate. For example, the caption for Figure 2 explains the behavior of the classification accuracy as a function of training epoch when a part of the labels is randomized. The figure references are consistent with the text, and the tables are well-organized with clear labels and headers. However, the visual content of the figures cannot be assessed due to the text-only input modality.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-FIG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"62dd85846caa90eb33121d4da6bd7c84ae90e24e4669